00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:10.870 align:start position:0%
the abalone spend their first six months  in the farms hatchery in nursery pond at  six months of age the abalone is  graduate to the cultivation pod after  six months to a year in the cultivation  pond the abalone e's are mature and  ready for harvesting workers remove them  from the shell and remove organs to be  used for other products then the workers  prepare to extract collagen from the  meat first they mash the meat in an  industrial sized blender the trick is to  use an extraction method that doesn't  destroy the collagen or diminish its  effectiveness abalone collagen must have  full potency when consumed in order to  stimulate the human body to produce more  of its own collagen since prolonged  heating turns collagen into gelatin  workers use a process called cold  extraction stirring the meat in  refrigerated tanks for up to seven days  until the collagen separates and rises  to the top  workers skim off the collagen then to  make this particular product blend it  with mixed fruit juices  then they heat the drink in  pasteurization tanks for three minutes  to kill off any bacteria the drink  contains 20% collagen and 80% chews when  it's time to package the product the  conveyor belt moves glass bottles to the  cleaning station which washes them out  with pressurized boiling water after  washing the bottles move to the next  machine which fills them with the drink  the next machine seals the bottles with  an aluminium twist cap  controlled by a sensor an inkjet printer  applies the lock number on the cap along  with the products expiration date a year  away while this drink is a skin  enhancement product other abalone  collagen formulations are designed for  weight loss boosting immunity increasing  bone density and strengthening cartilage
 

